  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nThe upper ridge will slowly shift eastward and give way to\nsouthwest flow aloft this evening through the weekend. There is\npotential for strong thunderstorms in the southeast this evening\nand in the east tomorrow afternoon. The upper trough will move in\nto bring temperatures down and precipitation will move in for the\nweekend. A few hundredths in the southwest up to 1 inch in the\nnortheast are possible through Sunday night. The GEFS and ECMWF\nensembles suggest an upper ridge will move in during the early\nparts of next week. They also suggest an upper trough over the\nPacific Northwest will influence the area by the middle of the\nweek to bring temperatures down and move back toward southwest\nflow.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nOnly deviation to NBM was to tweak PoPs from now through Saturday\nevening.\n\nThere is high confidence in areas north of the Missouri River to\nsee amounts between one tenth of an inch of rain up to 1 inch from\nnow through Sunday night, and south of the river below 0.5 \ninches.\n\nThere is low to moderate confidence of a thunderstorms producing\ngusts over 50 mph this evening and tomorrow evening.",
